<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_features",
    "P2P lobby invites and Arcade links appear as rich session cards instead of a plain line with a link."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_p2p}>{dgettext("help_features", "What the Card Shows")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_features",
    "A card names who created the session and walks through its lifecycle on a small timeline: when it was created, when it connected (P2P) or the game started (Arcade), and — once it is over — when it ended, how long it ran, and why it closed."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_btn_join}>{dgettext("help_features", "Live vs. Finished")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_features",
    "While a session is still live the card offers a button — Join or Open lobby for P2P, Open Arcade for a game. Once the session has finished the card shows its final state and drops the button."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_document_alert}>{dgettext("help_features", "Notes")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_features",
    "If a session can no longer be found (for example, an old invite whose session was purged), the card falls back to the plain join link."
  )}
</p>
